1
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,159
Let go of me!

2
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,479
Get your hands off me!

3
00:00:52,479 --> 00:00:53,880
Thanks, model citizen.

4
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,079
Getting involved again, huh?

5
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:59,000
You okay?

6
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:01,759
If you're fine, I'll head back to interrogate him.

7
00:01:02,119 --> 00:01:03,280
Hey, Captain Lu.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,920
Have you eaten?

9
00:01:05,319 --> 00:01:06,599
I'm good, no need.

10
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,599
Don't be so distant.

11
00:01:08,959 --> 00:01:09,760
Excuse me, Granny.

12
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,200
Yes?

13
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,920
Pack up ten bowls of noodles for me.

14
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:13,319
I'll pay for all of it.

15
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,319
Oh, no need!

16
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,400
Xiao Lu and his officers

17
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,120
keep us ordinary folks safe.

18
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,200
I can't take money for this meal.

19
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,640
Oh, that won't do!

20
00:01:21,959 --> 00:01:22,519
Granny,

21
00:01:22,519 --> 00:01:23,560
here's the thing.

22
00:01:23,719 --> 00:01:24,959
A quick word with you.

23
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,319
Having him as your assistant

24
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:29,400
is actually pretty good.

25
00:01:29,959 --> 00:01:31,319
Once the interrogation wraps up,

26
00:01:31,519 --> 00:01:32,359
I'll be in touch.

27
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:33,400
All right.

28
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,599
Granny, you see,

29
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,920
you really must take this money.

30
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,920
It's my only chance to show what I can do.

31
00:01:43,359 --> 00:01:44,400
Thank you so much.

32
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,400
Alright, alright.

33
00:01:47,239 --> 00:01:47,959
Thanks, Granny.

34
00:01:58,319 --> 00:01:59,879
Leaving already, Captain Lu?

35
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,400
You haven't even grabbed your food yet.

36
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,439
Everything looks fine.

37
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,759
Having a man in the house makes a difference.

38
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:17,280
There's so much more masculine energy.

39
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:18,520
Stop talking nonsense.

40
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:19,879
It's not like you live here.

41
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:23,120
Are you saying...

42
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,919
you want me to stay at your place?

43
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,199
What did you say to Grandma...

44
00:02:29,199 --> 00:02:30,719
...that made her take your money?

45
00:02:32,919 --> 00:02:34,240
I told her...

46
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,360
...to give me a chance to impress you.

47
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,840
Good night, honey.

48
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,960
According to police reports,

49
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,319
regarding the pregnant woman case in Ancheng City,

50
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:58,560
progress has been made in the investigation.

51
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,360
Suspect Yang Xiaotian has been arrested.

52
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,680
The public is eagerly awaiting the truth.

53
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:04,879
I didn't kill her!

54
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:06,360
I didn't kill anyone!

55
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,560
She was already dead when I got there!

56
00:03:08,719 --> 00:03:10,280
I'm being framed!

57
00:03:10,599 --> 00:03:11,479
Yang Xiaotian,

58
00:03:11,479 --> 00:03:13,719
if you merely found her dead,

59
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:15,439
why didn't you call the police right away,

60
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,960
instead of running off?

61
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:18,479
I have a criminal record!

62
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,199
When I walked in

63
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:21,680
and saw she was already dead,

64
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,919
I knew I was being set up as a scapegoat!

65
00:03:23,919 --> 00:03:24,960
If I didn't run,

66
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,400
was I supposed to wait around for you to arrest me?

67
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,439
Wu Qimeng texted him,

68
00:03:35,439 --> 00:03:36,719
telling him to come over that night.

69
00:03:36,719 --> 00:03:38,199
The text sent from Wu Qimeng's phone

70
00:03:38,199 --> 00:03:39,199
was deleted,

71
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:40,919
but the record remains on Yang Xiaotian's phone.

72
00:03:41,439 --> 00:03:42,759
We also got confirmation

73
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:43,800
from the telecom company.

74
00:03:44,439 --> 00:03:46,000
At 8:40 p.m.,

75
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,960
Wu Qimeng sent Yang Xiaotian a message.

76
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,000
It read,

77
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,159
"My husband isn't home tonight.

78
00:03:50,159 --> 00:03:51,120
Come over to my place.

79
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,960
I have a surprise for you."

80
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,400
Did Yang Xiaotian confess?

81
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,879
That's the tricky part of the interrogation.

82
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,360
All the evidence, timeline, and motive point to him,

83
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:01,039
yet Yang Xiaotian refuses to admit guilt,

84
00:04:01,039 --> 00:04:02,319
insisting he was framed.

85
00:04:02,599 --> 00:04:04,159
Send me the interrogation footage.

86
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:05,159
Already sent it.

87
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,719
Although we urgently need to solve this

88
00:04:06,719 --> 00:04:07,719
and give the public answers,

89
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,039
we can't frame an innocent person either.

90
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,800
Understood.

91
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:17,000
Why did you kill Wu Qimeng?

92
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,959
I didn't kill her!

93
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,800
I didn't kill her!

94
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,240
I didn't kill her!

95
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,680
She invited me over!

96
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,519
Why won't you believe

97
00:04:27,519 --> 00:04:29,079
what I'm saying?

98
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:34,199
Why did you kill Wu Qimeng?

99
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,879
I didn't kill her!

100
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:39,240
I didn't kill her!

101
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,600
She invited me over!

102
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:43,160
Why won't you believe

103
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,839
what I'm saying?

104
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,360
After prolonged routine questioning,

105
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,279
when hit with the core question,

106
00:04:50,279 --> 00:04:52,000
if he tried to keep lying,

107
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:53,519
it would be very hard to conceal.

108
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,800
Yang Xiaotian's reaction—

109
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:59,319
shaking his head while denying—

110
00:04:59,399 --> 00:05:01,240
shows his words and body language are aligned.

111
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,079
As simple as that may seem,

112
00:05:03,319 --> 00:05:05,120
under prolonged high-pressure interrogation,

113
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,839
very few people can keep their words and actions aligned.

114
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,759
Often, while denying verbally,

115
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:10,199
they subconsciously nod.

116
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,519
Still, this is merely our hypothesis.

117
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,839
It cannot serve as proof

118
00:05:16,839 --> 00:05:18,040
that Yang Xiaotian isn't lying.

119
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,199
True, Yang Xiaotian is a serial thief,

120
00:05:21,639 --> 00:05:22,639
slick and worldly.

121
00:05:23,399 --> 00:05:24,319
Most people, upon seeing a corpse,

122
00:05:24,319 --> 00:05:25,480
would instinctively call the police.

123
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,120
Yet his first reaction was that he was being framed.

124
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:29,839
He's either remarkably clever,

125
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
or trained specifically to resist interrogation.

126
00:05:34,439 --> 00:05:35,480
We need other methods

127
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,680
to test Yang Xiaotian.

128
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:40,879
Let's head to the police interrogation room.

129
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:41,920
Okay.

130
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:55,480
Gu Yan works with our police force

131
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,959
as a criminal psychologist,

132
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,800
so for the interrogation room,

133
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:00,040
only she's allowed inside.

134
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:05,480
Come here.

135
00:06:20,199 --> 00:06:21,439
What did you tell him?

136
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,759
You'll find out soon enough.

137
00:06:32,279 --> 00:06:33,879
Around 176 centimeters tall,

138
00:06:34,199 --> 00:06:35,399
lean build,

139
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:38,040
weathered by years of outdoor work,

140
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,600
dark skin, slouchy and brazen posture.

141
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,920
A slick operator seasoned by the streets.

142
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,160
Yang Xiaotian.

143
00:06:44,639 --> 00:06:46,480
Since you claim you're not the killer,

144
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,000
then cooperate fully with the police.

145
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,360
I am cooperating!

146
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,360
But if you can't catch the killer,

147
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,480
you still won't catch him.

148
00:06:57,279 --> 00:06:58,839
When pressure comes from higher-ups,

149
00:07:00,079 --> 00:07:01,560
just to give everyone an answer

150
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,399
and rush to close the case,

151
00:07:02,399 --> 00:07:03,959
you'll just pin it on me! Frame me!

152
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,120
Yang Xiaotian.

153
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:08,040
Stop your baseless, malicious accusations.

154
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,240
If the police operated like that,

155
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,040
I wouldn't be sitting in front of you.

156
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:17,079
We won't frame an innocent person,

157
00:07:17,079 --> 00:07:18,680
nor will we let a criminal get away.

158
00:07:19,879 --> 00:07:20,920
We need you to realize

159
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,199
the gravity of this case.

160
00:07:22,839 --> 00:07:24,920
When all the evidence points to you,

161
00:07:25,079 --> 00:07:26,040
you should understand

162
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,600
we're the only ones who haven't given up on you.

163
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,560
If you want to clear your name

164
00:07:29,839 --> 00:07:30,959
and get out of here sooner,

165
00:07:31,279 --> 00:07:33,120
you'd better answer my questions properly.

166
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,040
Fine.

167
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:42,839
I'll cooperate.

168
00:07:47,319 --> 00:07:48,639
In your family,

169
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,240
who were you closest to?

170
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,480
I was closest to my grandma.

171
00:07:53,959 --> 00:07:55,480
Though she passed away a long time ago.

172
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,000
Then between you and your grandma,

173
00:07:57,199 --> 00:07:58,879
what is your most vivid memory?

174
00:08:04,519 --> 00:08:05,959
Gaze shifts up first,

175
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,480
then down to the left.

176
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,759
Typical eye movement when recalling memories.

177
00:08:11,399 --> 00:08:12,399
When I was a kid,

178
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:15,920
I lived with my grandparents.

179
00:08:17,199 --> 00:08:18,800
Back when I was in elementary school,

180
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,319
our house was pretty far from school.

181
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,360
I remember it rained one day—

182
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:25,839
a torrential downpour.

183
00:08:26,319 --> 00:08:27,959
You know, back then, around my house,

184
00:08:27,959 --> 00:08:29,439
the roads were pure mud,

185
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,519
all rutted and bumpy,

186
00:08:30,519 --> 00:08:31,439
really hard to walk on.

187
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,320
My grandma put on a pair of...

188
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,960
a pair of farming boots for working the fields,

189
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,960
and carried me on her back.

190
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,600
She draped a raincoat over me

191
00:08:41,679 --> 00:08:44,039
and carried me all the way to school.

192
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,240
Except on...

193
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:50,360
her way back, she slipped and took a bad fall.

194
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,080
Ever since then,

195
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:55,080
her back was never the same.

196
00:08:59,799 --> 00:09:01,080
My poor grandma...

197
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,679
She suffered her whole life

198
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,360
and never got to enjoy a single good day.

199
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,840
You have two prior arrests

200
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,240
and convictions for theft.

201
00:09:13,879 --> 00:09:14,720
Let me ask you:

202
00:09:15,399 --> 00:09:17,360
have you stolen anything in the past two years,

203
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,840
just without getting caught?

204
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,240
Eyes darting to the right again.

205
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,759
Trying to fabricate an excuse to deceive me.

206
00:09:24,759 --> 00:09:26,519
He's lying.

207
00:09:27,919 --> 00:09:28,720
No.

208
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:30,879
I really haven't.

209
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,080
Really.

210
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,279
I swear.

211
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,399
That's the absolute truth.

212
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:37,080
I've really gone straight.

213
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,879
When lying,

214
00:09:41,159 --> 00:09:43,200
he subconsciously repeats his words

215
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,279
and stares right at me,

216
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,960
trying to make me believe him.

217
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,240
This kid

218
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,679
has no professional anti-interrogation training.

219
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,279
On the day of the crime,

220
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,840
after 8:30 p.m.,

221
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,159
what were your movements?

222
00:09:57,799 --> 00:09:59,360
I do know that pregnant woman.

223
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:01,279
I delivered packages to her place a few times.

224
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,559
Once, when she had morning sickness,

225
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,159
I even drove her to the hospital.

226
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:07,440
At 8:40 that night,

227
00:10:07,759 --> 00:10:09,240
she sent me a text.

228
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:10,399
She said

229
00:10:10,519 --> 00:10:11,799
her husband wasn't home

230
00:10:11,799 --> 00:10:12,799
and told me to come over.

231
00:10:12,799 --> 00:10:14,159
She said she had a surprise for me.

232
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:23,759
I... I know my thoughts were dirty,

233
00:10:24,159 --> 00:10:25,799
but she was just so gorgeous.

234
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:27,840
An angel like that from a good family...

235
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,320
Why would she ever fall for someone like me?

236
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:32,279
It would've been the blessing of a lifetime.

237
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,960
As it turned out,

238
00:10:36,159 --> 00:10:38,360
that kind of luck never comes my way.

239
00:10:39,879 --> 00:10:41,639
I didn't bring an umbrella when I went,

240
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,200
so I got completely soaked in the rain.

241
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,639
When I hurried over,

242
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,679
her door was left slightly ajar.

243
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,759
The living room lights were off,

244
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,799
but there was light in the bedroom.

245
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:10,399
Miss?

246
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:13,000
Miss?

247
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:14,559
Miss?

248
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:19,000
Haven't seen you in a while since the hospital.

249
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,360
Miss?

250
00:11:23,799 --> 00:11:25,519
Did you have your eye on me all along?

251
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,720
I might not have much going for me,

252
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,399
but I've got plenty of strength.

253
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,000
Did I get the wrong idea?

254
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,679
It's okay.

255
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,519
If something's going on,

256
00:11:46,519 --> 00:11:47,879
you can always tell me.

257
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,159
I felt something was off.

258
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,559
I leaned in to take a look,

259
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,399
and saw her face looked completely off.

260
00:11:54,399 --> 00:11:55,240
Miss?

261
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,559
Looking further down,

262
00:11:56,559 --> 00:11:57,879
I saw on her neck

263
00:11:57,879 --> 00:11:59,360
a ring of strangle marks.

264
00:11:59,399 --> 00:12:00,320
Miss?

265
00:12:02,039 --> 00:12:02,759
Miss?

266
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,120
Miss!
